{
  "slug": "artist:headhunterz",
  "name": "Headhunterz",
  "editorial_article": "Born in Veenendaal, Netherlands in 1985, Willem Rebergen pioneered the global rise of hardstyle as Headhunterz, famously winning the Defqon.1 DJ contest in 2004 under his earlier alias, Nasty D-Tuners. His early production success was heavily nurtured by The Prophet, who signed him to Scantraxx in 2005. The 2008 debut album Project One, a collaborative effort with Wildstylez featuring tracks like 'The Art of Creation' and 'Life Beyond Earth', became a foundational influence on the genre through its trance-leaning melodies and heavy pitched kicks. After briefly pivoting toward house-influenced sounds and signing with Ultra Music in 2013, Rebergen returned to his roots at the 2017 Defqon.1 Festival. He later co-founded the label Art of Creation in 2018 with Wildstylez. Despite an indefinite break from live touring beginning in late 2023, he continued to top the Q-dance Hardstyle Top-100 poll, winning five times including three consecutive victories with 'Live Forever' in 2024.",
